# Capstone code standards (summary)

- **Comments:** Remove comments that only repeat the code or name. Keep at most one short line for non-obvious *why* or invariants that naming cannot carry.
- **Naming:** Prefer descriptive classes, functions, and variables over comments. Conventional ML names (`X_train`, `y_val`, etc.) are fine.
- **Notebooks:** Narrative in markdown cells; avoid long `#` blocks in code that duplicate markdown.
- **Scope:** Do not edit `docs/study/`, `docs/course/`, `docs/submissions/`, or `churn-prediction/reports/` for “style cleanup” unless the user asks.

For a full checklist and pre-push workflow, read [.cursor/skills/capstone-code-standards/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/capstone-code-standards/SKILL.md).
